        <h2 id="gu-what-heading" class="text-balance text-[#111827] text-[28px] sm:text-[32px] lg:text-[36px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight">Instead of describing the answer, the software builds it.</h2>
        <p data-aeo="answer" class="mt-6 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-[#374151]"><strong class="font-medium text-[#111827]">Generative UI is an interface composed at runtime</strong> by a model choosing and filling components from your own design system.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">It is used for dashboards, adaptive forms, internal tools and in-product assistants: anywhere a user knows what they want but not where it lives.</p>
        <dl class="mt-8 space-y-5">
          <div class="border-l-2 border-amber-400 pl-4"><dt class="font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-700">The problem</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#374151]">Most software makes people learn where things live. Chat helps, but it answers in text, and the user still goes somewhere else to do the work.</dd></div>
          <div class="border-l-2 border-[#76B900] pl-4"><dt class="font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#3d6600]">The idea</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#374151]">A model reads the request and assembles the screen for it: real components from your design system, filled with live data, with the controls attached.</dd></div>
          <div class="border-l-2 border-[#111827] pl-4"><dt class="font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#111827]">The guardrail</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#374151]">It can only use components you have approved, with props a schema validates. It never writes markup, so your design system and permissions stay in charge.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>

